# Allowlist for both build contexts that use this file:
#  (a) this checkout as context (containers/onprem/platform.Dockerfile): code and the lock only. Root file on purpose: the legacy
#      builder ignores <Dockerfile>.dockerignore, and .platform/ holds project capabilities and credentials. Keeps .platform/,
#      runs/, outputs/, incoming/, web/, .venv/ and .env out of the build context.
#  (b) the on-prem images' context SRC holding this repository as workcell/ and panoptes-serving as serving/ (docker/*.Dockerfile);
#      scripts/onprem/stage_context.sh copies this file to SRC/.dockerignore. Never outputs/ (24 GB), .venv/, node_modules/, runs,
#      weights or .git. Patterns of the other context match nothing there and are harmless.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!ehs_spatial/
!panoptes_worker/
!scripts/
!containers/onprem/serve_publications.py
!workcell/docker
!workcell/scripts
!workcell/modal_apps
!workcell/configs
!serving/scripts
!serving/modal_apps
!serving/ehs_spatial
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.venv
**/node_modules
**/outputs
**/.git
**/.DS_Store
